## Verify Configuration Before Boot

Before booting compute nodes, verify that BSS and cloud-init are configured
correctly. These checks catch the most common failures before a wasted boot
cycle.

First, confirm that BSS has the correct kernel parameters stored:

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Verify BSS boot params are uploaded -->
```bash
ochami -k bss boot params get \
	| grep -q "ds=nocloud-net" \
	&& echo "BSS: OK" \
	|| { echo "BSS: FAILED - check boot params"; exit 1; }
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->

Next, confirm that the cloud-init default configuration was uploaded
successfully:

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Verify cloud-init defaults are uploaded -->
```bash
ochami -k cloud-init defaults get \
	| grep -q "base-url" \
	&& echo "cloud-init defaults: OK" \
	|| { echo "cloud-init defaults: FAILED"; exit 1; }
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->

Finally, confirm that the compute group cloud-init configuration is present.
This is what delivers the SSH keys and munge key to the node at boot:

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Verify cloud-init compute group is uploaded -->
```bash
ochami -k cloud-init group get raw compute \
	| grep -q "compute" \
	&& echo "cloud-init group: OK" \
	|| { echo "cloud-init group: FAILED"; exit 1; }
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->

